{
  "module": "MLaneOwed.tla",
  "status": "refinement",
  "summary": "A task that finds a lane to the core full (net.rs publish, Link::owe / Link::consumed; record 0046): try, mark `owed`, try again; the consumer that takes a value swaps the mark and notifies. A held packet has no bound: it is delivered once the core takes values, with no tick, or its task is cancelled. A held receipt is published or ends the task with its queue-full code after RESULT_WAIT, by the tick.",
  "issues": [648],
  "tests": ["mqttiumd/crates/mqttiumd/src/net.rs", "mqttiumd/crates/mqttiumd/src/net/reactor.rs"],
  "replays": [{"file": "mqttiumd/crates/mqttiumd/src/net.rs", "test": "input_saturation_is_backpressure_and_loses_no_packet"}, {"file": "mqttiumd/crates/mqttiumd/src/net.rs", "test": "cancellation_ends_idle_and_partial_socket_tasks"}, {"file": "mqttiumd/crates/mqttiumd/src/net/reactor.rs", "test": "a_notification_runs_the_task_once_and_a_waiting_task_is_ticked"}],
  "not_replayed": "The counterexample of mut-single-attempt (the consumer empties the lane between the first attempt and the mark) needs a chosen schedule of the core and reactor threads; no deterministic test replays it, and the 5 ms tick hides it from a timing test (mut-single-attempt-ticked passes). No test lets a receipt wait for RESULT_WAIT (reach-queue-full-end).",
  "configs": [
    {"config": "MLaneOwed-safety-packet.cfg", "expect": "pass", "invariants": ["TypeOK", "LaneBounded", "NoLostOwed", "EndedOnlyAfterDeadline", "PacketNeverEndsTask", "CancelRunsTask"]},
